                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 37-year-old male, who presented on 02/08/2005 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever. Clinical examination revealed rebound tenderness at McBurney's point. Blood tests demonstrated leukocytosis consistent with acute inflammation. Abdominal ultrasonography confirmed the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. The patient was prepared for surgery without delay. A laparoscopic appendectomy was performed successfully on 02/08/2005 without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, the patient received intravenous antibiotics, analgesics, and fluid replacement. Wound healing was satisfactory, and the patient remained afebrile. He was discharged on 04/08/2005 in good general condition. Outpatient follow-up in two weeks is recommended. Please do not hesitate to contact me should any questions arise.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
